{#
  CASE STUDY LAYOUT — the new design. Shared by every case study built to it:
  ONTON (193:4660) and Challenquiz (281:64068) so far.

  A SEPARATE FILE FROM layouts/case-study.njk ON PURPOSE. That one is the v2
  shell — it renders NOTHING now that Ezam is retired, but it is what the three
  pages looked like before this file: a "← All projects" header, a
  <dl> of Client/Role/Year/Domain, a .progress-bar with no driver, and a "View
  All Projects" footer button. 193:4660 has none of those — no back link, no
  meta list, no sidebar, no table of contents, no reading-progress bar. It is
  the site header, a stack of full-bleed ruled bands, and the site footer.
  Bending the old layout into that shape would have meant making every piece of
  it conditional; leaving it alone keeps two working pages working.

  WHAT THIS FILE OWNS is only the shell. The bands themselves live in each page
  (src/work/<slug>.njk) because their structure is specific to the write-up,
  and every string lives in _data/<slug>.js. The other shared parts are the
  .case scope in tokens.css and _case-study-v2.css.

  data-header-theme="light": the page is white top to bottom, so the header
  stays on its light palette for all of it. The footer carries its own "dark"
  and flips it back on the way past.

  pageId IS DECLARED BY THE PAGE, NOT HERE, and that is what lets one layout
  serve several case studies. base.njk writes it to <body data-page>, and
  scripts/analytics-events.js reads exactly that attribute to decide what to
  fire and what to label it with — so each page sets its own slug and GA gets
  view_case_study / finish_case_study with case_study: "onton" or
  "challenquiz". Setting it here would collapse every page onto one identifier.

  That was precisely the bug layouts/case-study.njk had: it hardcodes
  `pageId: work`, so the page using it reported case_study: "work" rather than
  its own slug. Moot since Ezam was retired — that layout has no pages left — but
  worth knowing before anything is ever pointed at it again.
#}

